      "summary": "Advised by Prof. Huan Liu.",
      "highlights": [
        "LLM post-training & reasoning: reasoning distillation via explanatory data synthesis and RL with structured rewards; an RL-optimized knowledge-graph retriever for reasoning-augmented generation; a controlled synthetic environment for pre-training LLMs from scratch and probing CoT reasoning.",
        "LLM/MLLM security, privacy & safety: bilevel-optimized knowledge-poisoning attacks on RAG systems and covert malicious-agent injection into MLLM societies; adversarial data synthesis that protects data from unauthorized fine-tuning of LLMs and VLMs; RL-driven defenses that shield proprietary LLMs from unauthorized API-based knowledge distillation.",
        "RAG & LLM agent applications: knowledge-graph-grounded response verification in RAG for domain-specific question answering; a multi-agent RL framework in Graph-RAG for multi-hop reasoning; LLM multi-agent frameworks with human-in-the-loop collaboration for large-scale content analysis.",
        "LLM evaluation: LLM-as-a-judge and the detectability of LLM-generated judgments; detection and evaluation of LLM-generated content; evaluation of CoT reasoning under distribution shift.",
        "Causality, interpretability, efficiency & recommendation: causality-guided representation learning for robust generalization across domains, styles, and modalities; concept bottleneck models for interpretable open-ended grading; low-rank node-level graph diffusion for few-shot node classification; diffusion language models for bundle recommendation."
      ]
